    "text": "Let ABC be the triangle such that the equations of lines $A B$ and $A C$ be $3 y-x=2$ and $x+y=2$, respectively, and the points B and C lie on x -axis. If $P$ is the orthocentre of the triangle $A B C$, then the area of the triangle PBC is equal to",
